{"ts": "2026-09-08T15:43:07+00:00", "event": "incident", "what": "TOOLING DEFECT: sync_registry.py silently ignores NEW role packs. It prints 'registry synced from 121 packs' - a count of packs on disk - while its loop contains 'if slug not in by: continue', so a pack that is not already in roles.json is skipped and never registered. Two new roles appeared to sync successfully and were in fact registered nowhere. The message actively misleads.", "tried": "Ran sync_registry.py after adding two role packs; it reported success with 121 packs and 0 fields updated. roles.json still contained 119 entries and the DB still contained 119 agents.", "next": "Worked around by writing the roles.json entries and the agent + behavioral_contract rows directly, then re-running the full validation suite (companydb verify, company validate, staffing_audit, audit_org, cognitive_validation 23/23, capability_validation 14/14, behavior_tests 35/35, readiness_audit 43/43) and regenerating gen_memory.py and matrices.py. RECOMMENDED FIX: sync_registry.py should either add unknown packs or print a loud warning naming them. Owner: coo/founder - it is a governance mechanism and D-14 makes packs the source of truth, so silently dropping a pack breaks the stated contract."}
